#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""WP6 fixture generator — every qr_candidates test fixture, from scratch.

LAW (FINAL_PLAN.md section 6, and the rule WP3 already follows): "fixture files
live under engine/cpp/tests/fixtures/, generated by a committed script, never by
hand-editing binaries".  A corrupt fixture is built by ASKING this writer for the
corruption; nothing here pokes bytes into a good file afterwards.

INDEPENDENCE.  The event-signal sequence-root formula is implemented here a
SECOND time, in a second language, from the same primary source as the C++ port
(the frozen feasibility witness, source sha256
12cf894248a371cbc98d7b6d0a65ab0fc1fc359cbe1e36a8b7c927eb8c1f6d3b, whose framing
and kernel constants are published in side_prefix_feasibility_v1/probe_s125_v3/
receipt.json).  The roots this script writes into the fixture `t14_bounds.tsv`
are therefore an INDEPENDENT expectation: if the C++ reproduces them, two
separate implementations of the same primary source agree.  Nothing here reads
the C++ output, and the C++ never computes these numbers any other way.

Usage:
    python3 make_candidate_fixtures.py [--out-dir DIR] [--literals-path PATH]

Default out-dir is ``<this file>/candidates``.  Output is deterministic: two
runs are byte-identical.
"""

